1
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:08,400
Best Friends Take the Stage and Steal the Show!

2
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:10,800
Bratz: Rock Angelz is a animation, family, music
film directed by David Mucci Fassett.

3
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:13,200
After starting up their own teen magazine, Bratz girls Yasmin, Cloe,
Jade, and Sasha fly to London to cover a rock concert.

4
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:15,600
Yasmin (voice), played by Dionne Quan.

5
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:18,000
Cloe (voice), played by Olivia Hack.

6
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:20,400
Jade (voice), played by Soleil Moon Frye.

7
00:21:16,799 --> 00:21:22,799
Sasha (voice), played by Tia Mowry.

8
00:24:19,200 --> 00:24:25,200
Burdine Maxwell (voice), played by Wendie Malick.

9
00:27:21,600 --> 00:27:27,600
Kirstee (voice), played by Kaley Cuoco.

10
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:30,000
Bratz: Rock Angelz is a 2005 adventure video game based on the
Bratz fashion doll line and published by THQ.

11
00:33:26,400 --> 00:33:32,400
It is based on the direct-to-video film Bratz: Rock Angelz and
the line of dolls affiliated with the same name.

12
00:36:28,800 --> 00:36:34,800
The game was released for the PlayStation 2,
GameCube, Game Boy Advance, and Windows.

13
00:39:31,200 --> 00:39:37,200
Blitz Games developed the PlayStation 2 and GameCube versions, while Altron and AWE
Games developed the Game Boy Advance and Windows versions respectively.

14
00:42:33,599 --> 00:42:39,599
The game loosely follows the film's plot, where
the Bratz start a fashion magazine.

15
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:42,000
They later receive an invitation from a nightclub in London to perform at a
concert venue and outsell their rival competitor, Your Thing magazine.

16
00:48:38,400 --> 00:48:44,400
However, unlike the film, the Bratz travel to areas other than London.

17
00:51:40,800 --> 00:51:46,800
The gameplay primarily revolves around participating in tasks for
the magazine, as well as performing fashion shows.

18
00:54:43,200 --> 00:54:49,200
It also features a variety of minigames that consist
of posing, photography, and racing.

19
00:57:45,599 --> 00:57:51,599
Players can also dress the Bratz girls in various fashion
lines and apply makeup to their faces.

20
01:00:48,000 --> 01:00:54,000
Upon release, reviews of Bratz: Rock Angelz were generally mixed.

21
01:03:50,400 --> 01:03:56,400
Some critics praised the game for its open world,
minigames, and creative features.

22
01:06:52,800 --> 01:06:58,800
However, many others criticized it for its sole
appeal to a young female demographic.

23
01:09:55,199 --> 01:10:01,199
The game sold 1.5 million copies upon its release.

24
01:12:57,600 --> 01:13:03,600
It also received three sequels, which are titled Bratz: Forever Diamondz (2006),
Bratz: The Movie (2007), and Bratz: Girlz Really Rock (2008).
